# scripts/surface.allow: a function of the extensions that test/fuzz/surface_sweep.py cannot exercise in a mode (or must call with small integers). SIGNATURE TAB MODES TAB REASON
# SIGNATURE is pg_proc.oid::regprocedure; MODES: * (super, rollback, role), a comma list of them, no-huge (called with integers of at most 1000, the function runs or allocates as much as it is given; every _test_ function is called so).
# A function that is exercised in a listed mode, or that is gone, fails the sweep: delete the row.
sift.approx_count_distinct_trans(internal,anyelement)	*	internal sketch state cannot be built from SQL; every call of the aggregate sift.approx_count_distinct in the sweep runs it
sift.approx_count_distinct_final(internal)	*	internal sketch state cannot be built from SQL; every call of the aggregate sift.approx_count_distinct in the sweep runs it
sift.approx_count_distinct_combine(internal,internal)	*	internal sketch states cannot be built from SQL; runs only in a parallel aggregate plan, which test/sql/col_approx.sql compares with the serial one
sift.approx_count_distinct_serial(internal)	*	internal sketch state cannot be built from SQL; runs only in a parallel aggregate plan, which test/sql/col_approx.sql compares with the serial one
sift.approx_count_distinct_deserial(bytea,internal)	*	internal sketch state cannot be built from SQL; runs only in a parallel aggregate plan, which test/sql/col_approx.sql compares with the serial one
sift.sift_handler(internal)	*	index access method handler (internal result struct): SQL cannot call it; every CREATE INDEX USING sift of the sweep runs it
sift.col_handler(internal)	*	index access method handler (internal result struct): SQL cannot call it; every CREATE INDEX USING sift_col of the sweep runs it
sift.table_handler(internal)	*	table access method handler (internal result struct): SQL cannot call it; every CREATE TABLE USING sift_table of the sweep runs it
sift.values_handler(internal)	*	table access method handler of the value store (internal result struct): SQL cannot call it; the value store of every sift_col index of the sweep runs it
